00:26:00.700 --> 00:26:09.480
- Commander, she's doing her job.

00:26:09.480 --> 00:26:10.880
- She's gonna hurt herself.

00:26:10.880 --> 00:26:12.510
- Take my advice.

00:26:12.510 --> 00:26:14.850
Don't interfere.

00:26:14.850 --> 00:26:18.070
- I can't believe I'm getting this from you now.

00:26:18.070 --> 00:26:20.750
Has everyone on this ship gone crazy?

00:26:20.750 --> 00:26:23.590
- Not everyone.

00:26:23.590 --> 00:26:25.440
- Oh, I'm crazy.

00:26:25.440 --> 00:26:26.870
- It's not your fault.

00:26:26.870 --> 00:26:28.820
As far as I know, there are no species in the galaxy

00:26:28.820 --> 00:26:30.000
that have mastered the art

00:26:31.210 --> 00:26:31.710
Romance.

00:26:33.610 --> 00:26:36.560
Last one, they should be giving me a lecture.

00:26:38.040 --> 00:26:39.420
All the neural pressure was your idea.

00:26:39.520 --> 00:26:41.020
You were having trouble sleeping.

00:26:43.910 --> 00:26:48.520
What the hell am I going to do?

00:26:49.100 --> 00:26:53.150
This is one ailment that is universally untreatable.

00:26:54.430 --> 00:26:55.510
You'll have to suffer through it.

00:27:07.550 --> 00:27:19.530
been here before he's right we're going in circles trying to stop us how they're

00:27:19.530 --> 00:27:24.760
not letting us see the path to the surface how could that be possible it's

00:27:24.760 --> 00:27:25.800
time to come back

00:27:30.540 --> 00:27:31.140
I can't.

00:27:31.900 --> 00:27:33.600
We're fighting a war.

00:27:34.980 --> 00:27:36.000
Do you want to be a part of that?

00:27:36.570 --> 00:27:37.990
I don't want to fight anyone.

00:27:38.110 --> 00:27:39.070
I want to help my brother.

00:27:39.800 --> 00:27:42.510
Help him by standing up for what we believe in.

00:27:43.090 --> 00:27:44.490
She's doing what she thinks is right.

00:27:45.170 --> 00:27:46.310
She's betraying her people.

00:27:47.180 --> 00:27:47.800
That's not true.

00:27:49.730 --> 00:27:51.890
Shouldn't she be allowed to follow her own conscience?

00:27:52.400 --> 00:27:54.330
She's not following her conscience.

00:27:54.810 --> 00:27:55.330
How do you know?

00:27:56.000 --> 00:27:56.700
Have you read her mind?

00:27:57.510 --> 00:27:59.920
I thought that was against your custom.

00:28:02.780 --> 00:28:04.000
Jamel?

00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:07.400
Take my thoughts.

00:28:07.400 --> 00:28:19.180
You're certain this is what you want?

00:28:19.180 --> 00:28:20.930
Yes.

00:28:43.850 --> 00:28:51.200
Captain Starlog supplemental we've returned to Enterprise where we received word that the cargo ship Ticonderoga is missing

00:28:51.200 --> 00:29:00.000
Anything on long-range sensors not yet. What's our ETA will be at their last known coordinates in six hours. Tell Malcolm to finish his update

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:03.840
to the targeting scanners if you run into that marauder again I want to make

00:29:03.840 --> 00:29:19.020
sure every shot counts understood report she's good to go whenever you're

00:29:19.020 --> 00:29:22.820
ready I'm ready captain

00:29:45.230 --> 00:29:46.090
50% spike.

00:29:48.080 --> 00:29:50.630
You feeling all right?

00:29:52.310 --> 00:29:56.080
We can stop anytime you like.

00:29:58.140 --> 00:30:00.000
It's strangely enjoyable.

00:30:06.880 --> 00:30:09.850
- Please max it out.

00:30:09.850 --> 00:30:12.720
- Is that good?

00:30:12.720 --> 00:30:14.030
- Very good.

00:30:14.030 --> 00:30:17.720
- Is there another test we can try?

00:30:17.720 --> 00:30:18.980
- Simulator course correction.

00:30:34.220 --> 00:30:53.820
the trouble shut it down captain Starlog supplement we've arrived at the last

00:30:53.820 --> 00:30:59.220
known coordinates of the Ticonderoga I'm picking up debris hole fragments

00:31:00.990 --> 00:31:01.790
nacelle casings

00:31:01.790 --> 00:31:04.580
several bodies

00:31:04.580 --> 00:31:05.670
human

00:31:05.670 --> 00:31:07.180
keep scanning

00:31:07.180 --> 00:31:10.220
try to find the marauder's warp signature

00:31:10.220 --> 00:31:14.980
is there any word from sick man?

00:31:16.800 --> 00:31:17.640
she's gonna be okay

00:31:17.640 --> 00:31:21.880
Phlox says it's too dangerous to try again

00:31:21.880 --> 00:31:25.820
looks like we went all the way to Andoria

00:31:25.820 --> 00:31:29.570
for nothing

00:31:42.030 --> 00:31:43.470
What happened?

00:31:43.470 --> 00:31:44.890
You had a convulsion.

00:31:44.890 --> 00:31:45.810
You're all right now.

00:31:45.810 --> 00:31:48.840
I was dreaming.

00:31:48.840 --> 00:31:54.960
I'm care of.

00:31:54.960 --> 00:31:57.160
Failed, didn't I?

00:31:57.160 --> 00:31:58.320
Ridiculous.

00:32:00.190 --> 00:32:08.000
kind of bravery is never a failure. I'm a commander in the Imperial Guard. Don't be afraid to go

00:32:08.000 --> 00:32:24.860
anywhere near that thing. Talos was a fortunate woman. I was the fortunate one. My brother's

00:32:24.860 --> 00:32:27.560
going to die, isn't he? I won't hear that from him.

00:32:32.240 --> 00:32:33.520
You make it look easy.

00:32:33.520 --> 00:32:43.250
Keep being strong for me.

00:32:43.250 --> 00:32:48.240
A ship's dropping out of war.

00:32:48.240 --> 00:32:50.200
It appears to be a Tellarite freighter.

00:32:50.200 --> 00:32:51.600
Tactical alert.

00:32:51.600 --> 00:32:54.330
Hail them.

00:32:54.330 --> 00:32:59.160
Target their engines.

00:33:00.670 --> 00:33:08.040
- If it is a freighter.

00:33:08.040 --> 00:33:13.090
- Your kilometers.

00:33:42.000 --> 00:33:49.730
too damn fast i can't get a target lock what's happening we're under attack i'm going to the

00:33:49.730 --> 00:34:00.000
bridge wait i feel him where do you think you're going i need to

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:01.450
the device I need to try again.

00:34:01.450 --> 00:34:04.370
I can't allow it, you barely survived the last attempts.

00:34:04.370 --> 00:34:05.570
I can reach him.

00:34:05.570 --> 00:34:07.300
We can make him stop.

00:34:07.300 --> 00:34:09.540
Better try.

00:34:11.460 --> 00:34:13.830
Enterprise is taking heavy damage.

00:34:13.830 --> 00:34:15.750
Target with the second drone.

00:34:15.750 --> 00:34:18.820
Attack vector 177.

00:34:18.820 --> 00:34:20.880
It may not be necessary.

00:34:20.880 --> 00:34:22.330
Follow my orders.

00:34:22.330 --> 00:34:25.120
Yes, Admiral.

00:34:31.980 --> 00:34:35.410
Another ship's approaching, bearing 016 Mark 12.

00:34:35.410 --> 00:34:38.010
An Andorian battlecruiser.

00:34:38.010 --> 00:34:38.900
It's a power.

00:34:38.900 --> 00:34:40.850
Its power signature is not Andorian.

00:34:40.850 --> 00:34:41.910
Target them!

00:34:41.910 --> 00:34:46.050
Captain, I'm picking up an energy reading from sickbay.

00:34:46.050 --> 00:34:49.490
It's the telepresence unit.

00:34:49.490 --> 00:34:51.370
Archer to sickbay, what's going on?

00:34:51.370 --> 00:34:55.060
Jamel's going to make another attempt.

00:34:55.060 --> 00:34:56.050
Is she up to it?

00:34:56.050 --> 00:34:58.480
She's quite insistent.

00:35:14.110 --> 00:35:15.630
It could trigger a seizure.

00:35:15.630 --> 00:35:20.590
You can do it.

00:35:20.590 --> 00:35:21.960
Disconnect her.

00:35:21.960 --> 00:35:22.960
Now!

00:35:22.960 --> 00:35:23.780
No!

00:35:23.780 --> 00:35:24.780
She can do this!

00:35:24.780 --> 00:35:27.980
They've lost warp power.

00:35:27.980 --> 00:35:29.990
Continue targeting their engines.

00:35:31.560 --> 00:35:33.860
Someone's tapping into the telemetric array!

00:35:37.270 --> 00:35:38.330
Shumel?

00:35:39.940 --> 00:35:41.560
It's me.

00:35:41.960 --> 00:35:43.650
Possible?

00:35:43.840 --> 00:35:44.630
How?

00:35:45.610 --> 00:35:47.650
You have to stop what you're doing.

00:35:48.330 --> 00:35:49.170
Where are you?

00:35:50.080 --> 00:35:52.120
The ship you're attacking.

00:36:00.120 --> 00:36:14.960
are coming to a stop. We're defenseless. I've stopped firing. I thought you were dead. They said

00:36:14.960 --> 00:36:27.720
I was the last surviving Enon. They lied to you. I've killed so many people. It wasn't you. It was

00:36:27.720 --> 00:36:29.020
them they forced you.

00:36:31.340 --> 00:36:33.610
You can stop it.

00:36:33.610 --> 00:36:38.170
You know what you have to do.

00:36:38.170 --> 00:36:47.690
First drone is targeting the second.

00:36:47.690 --> 00:36:49.530
Take all weapons offline.

00:36:49.530 --> 00:36:52.160
I've lost access.

00:36:52.160 --> 00:36:58.660
Attacking each other.

00:36:58.660 --> 00:36:59.960
Let's give them a hand.

00:37:00.160 --> 00:37:02.160
Photonic torpedoes, full spread.

00:37:02.160 --> 00:37:03.160
Aye, sir.

00:37:03.160 --> 00:37:07.080
Stop this.

00:37:07.080 --> 00:37:08.840
Now.

00:37:08.840 --> 00:37:10.040
No!

00:37:10.040 --> 00:37:12.540
Resume your attack on the Earth ship.

00:37:12.540 --> 00:37:15.770
Remember me, Jamel.

00:37:15.770 --> 00:37:19.240
Gareth?

00:38:13.020 --> 00:38:17.830
Starlog supplemental there's been no sign of any other Marauder ships we're

00:38:17.830 --> 00:38:22.150
returning Shran and Jamel to Andorian I want to thank you again

00:38:22.150 --> 00:38:28.740
for you thanks and come with you my brother would have died alone

00:38:31.210 --> 00:38:39.570
- Goodbye, Captain. - Goodbye.

00:38:39.570 --> 00:38:45.020
I regret much of what happened between us recently.

00:38:45.020 --> 00:38:46.900
Same here.

00:38:46.900 --> 00:38:50.610
When you lose your ship, you aren't usually rewarded with another one.

00:38:50.610 --> 00:38:52.810
I may not see you for a while.

00:38:52.810 --> 00:38:57.420
If there's anything we can do or say on your behalf.

00:38:57.420 --> 00:38:58.800
I appreciate the offer.

00:39:00.120 --> 00:39:01.600
Let's just see what the future grows.

00:39:06.820 --> 00:39:11.940
Try to stay out of trouble, thanks kid.

00:39:21.760 --> 00:39:24.530
Come in.

00:39:26.430 --> 00:39:29.160
I've been looking over your report.

00:39:30.760 --> 00:39:32.240
I think you're being a little hard on yourself.

00:39:33.900 --> 00:39:35.130
There's no getting around it.

00:39:36.470 --> 00:39:38.710
I missed a 10-degree variance in the telepresence emitter.

00:39:39.030 --> 00:39:39.990
I spoke with Phlox.

00:39:40.760 --> 00:39:43.180
He doesn't think it had anything to do with Jamal's seizure.

00:39:43.900 --> 00:39:44.900
But he can't be sure.

00:39:46.890 --> 00:39:47.990
Either way, I should have caught it.

00:39:48.450 --> 00:39:49.970
We were all under a lot of pressure.

00:39:51.320 --> 00:39:52.540
My mind wasn't on the job.

00:39:53.360 --> 00:39:57.130
If that were true, we probably wouldn't be standing here now.

00:40:06.010 --> 00:40:06.910
Captain, I want to transfer.

00:40:10.830 --> 00:40:12.670
Where?

00:40:14.090 --> 00:40:16.690
The experienced people.

00:40:18.130 --> 00:40:21.550
You've turned them down twice before.

00:40:22.660 --> 00:40:23.180
Why now?

00:40:23.420 --> 00:40:25.510
I think I can do some good over there.

00:40:26.060 --> 00:40:28.430
I need you here, Tripp.

00:40:30.960 --> 00:40:31.640
They need me more.

00:40:33.870 --> 00:40:36.760
What's this really about?

00:40:36.980 --> 00:40:39.460
I told you.

00:40:40.250 --> 00:40:42.560
I haven't heard one thing that explains this.

00:40:45.510 --> 00:40:50.600
I said everything I want to.

00:40:52.230 --> 00:40:53.080
That's it.

00:40:58.600 --> 00:41:00.000
I'm supposed to accept...

00:41:04.800 --> 00:41:17.020
And if I refuse your transfer, I'm asking you to do this.

00:41:19.010 --> 00:41:24.990
It's your career trip, but as a friend, I'm asking you to stay.

00:41:27.870 --> 00:41:30.000
I can.

00:41:33.680 --> 00:41:39.960
All right. Thank you. Dismissed.
